# ===========================================================================
# Docker build context — backend image
#
# Everything excluded here is either a local artefact, a secret, or runtime
# state that is mounted as a volume instead of baked into the image. The build
# context is what gets uploaded to the Docker daemon, so an over-inclusive
# context is both slow and a leak risk: `.env` in particular must never be in
# it, and `.gitignore` has no effect on the Docker build context.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python virtualenvs and caches -----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# --- Frontend (built by its own image, not this one) -----------------------
frontend/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- Tests and local tooling ----------------------------------------------
tests/
notebooks/
.commandcode/

# --- Version control and CI ----------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Runtime state: mounted as volumes, never baked in ---------------------
# `data/` holds uploads and the SQLite fallback; `inventory-data/` is the
# mutable ERP system of record; `docs/` is the RAG corpus mounted read-only.
data/
inventory-data/
docs/

# --- Local binaries, logs, editor noise -----------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Deployment assets are not part of the application image --------------
deploy/
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose*.yml
aws.md
